description:
According to [Reuters](https://www.reuters.com/world/india/india-us-trade-deal-be-finalised-after-ustr-section-301-probe-india-trade-2026-06-08/), the United States and India are finalising talks on an interim trade deal with Washington.

> The two countries reached an [initial understanding](https://www.reuters.com/world/india/us-india-release-framework-an-interim-trade-deal-2026-02-06/) on a trade deal in February 2026, but negotiations slowed after U.S. President Donald Trump's sweeping tariff measures were struck ​down by the U.S. Supreme Court.
> &#x20;
> The US has since proposed an ​additional tariff of 12.5% on imports from India, and other countries, ⁠due to what Washington says is these countries' use of forced ​labour. It is also looking at imposing a separate tariff on India, claiming ​India has excess capacity in industries such as textiles and is exporting too much to the United States, damaging US industry.
> &#x20;
> &#x20;
> Bilateral trade [talks](https://www.reuters.com/world/india/india-us-near-trade-pact-tariff-terms-hinge-section-301-relief-source-says-2026-06-01/) gathered pace last week ​as a U.S. delegation led by Assistant US Trade ​Representative for ⁠South and Central Asia Brendan Lynch held three days of talks with Indian trade officials in New Delhi.
> &#x20;
> Last week, India's trade minister [Piyush Goyal said](https://www.reuters.com/world/india/first-tranche-us-india-trade-deal-likely-by-mid-july-says-india-trade-minister-2026-06-05/) the two ⁠sides ​were moving swiftly toward finalising the first ​tranche of a bilateral trade agreement that could be concluded by mid-July.

